    "finding_1_sensitivity_vs_precision": "Across all 10 validation patients, mean WT Recall is 96.4% while mean WT Precision is only 39.8%. Mean relative volume error is +184.2%, demonstrating that the model acts as an aggressive boundary expander rather than missing tumor voxels (mean FN is negligible compared to massive FP).",
    "finding_2_localization_to_label_2": "Decomposing WT predictions into sub-labels reveals that TC (Label 1 + Label 3) is well-bounded (TC Dice 0.6690, Precision 78.4%), whereas Label 2 (Peritumoral Edema) accounts for over 85% of all False Positive voxels. The model expands edema boundaries deeply into normal-appearing FLAIR white matter.",
    "finding_3_argmax_thresholding_weakness": "During inference, predictions are derived strictly via argmax(outputs, dim=1). Argmax forces discrete class assignment based on raw logit victory without requiring probability calibration. In glioblastomas where FLAIR hyperintensity fades gradually, background voxels with marginally positive edema logits are assigned Label 2. Class-specific probability thresholding (e.g. requiring P(Edema) > tau where tau in [0.65, 0.85]) is the primary candidate for controlled boundary contraction without retraining.",
    "finding_4_distillation_objective_dynamics": "Comparison across ablation models shows that Baseline UNETR (no distillation) had WT Dice of 0.7525, whereas Online Tokenizer (lambda_ot=2.0) dropped WT to 0.5324 while boosting TC (0.7022) and ET (0.7454). The auxiliary token alignment loss pushes ViT tokens toward high-contrast core semantics, causing the network to treat diffuse edema as secondary context and over-predicting its spatial extent."
